`,s.jsx(e.p,{children:s.jsx(e.em,{children:"Figure 1. The canonical Salus runtime architecture. The population path builds recoverable topology; the runtime hot path admits, evaluates, and guards current work; persistence, telemetry, replay, and recovery retain independent evidence."})}),`
`,s.jsx(e.p,{children:"The diagram is read left to right and top to bottom. External market, replay, protocol, pricing, and transport inputs enter through typed adapters. Configuration validates the control plane before it creates work. Population persists and hydrates topology into a warm catalogue; streaming ingestion updates current state without confusing it with durable topology. The hot path then scopes affected routes, prepares covered requests, evaluates them, selects or abstains, and passes only a guarded handoff to execution. State, observability, replay, and recovery are supporting owners rather than untracked side channels. Generic configuration and credential labels identify a boundary only; they do not reveal values or access material."}),`
